# m5_graze: the m2_play sweep (without its two holds) plus B held for updates 1960..1979,
# so the bar is spent before the ship meets bullets and a graze can show up in it (a full
# bar would cap the grant). 1959: game tick 1929, fuel 180, weapon F3 (03: the crates of
# M6 are collected at 803 and 1628 as in m2_play). 1979, the last held frame: 20 frames =
# 40 ticks, game tick 1889, fuel 140. 1980: PLAYING, no tick. The shifted sweep then
# brushes a bullet at update 2121 (game tick 2030) without being hit: grazes 0 -> 1 and
# fuel 154 -> 157 on that tick (the graze's 2 plus a refill). Refill alone cannot get there:
# 141 live ticks since the release (1889 -> 2030) give at most 140 + (9 + 141) / 10 = 155
# (9 = the most the refill counter can carry in), and the fuel is 157. No hit, rewinds 3.
# Until M6 the hold was 1964..1983; since the F2 crate kills faster, that timing slips past
# the bullet (grazes 0); four updates earlier brings the same graze back (same update).
--frames 2200 --dump-exports debug_state,debug_rewinds,debug_fuel,debug_grazes --at "1959 debug_state == 1" --at "1959 debug_game_tick == 1929" --at "1959 debug_fuel == 180" --at "1959 debug_weapon == 3" --at "1960 debug_state == 5" --at "1979 debug_game_tick == 1889" --at "1979 debug_fuel == 140" --at "1980 debug_state == 1" --at "2000 debug_history_check == 0" --at "2120 debug_grazes == 0" --at "2120 debug_fuel == 154" --at "2121 debug_game_tick == 2030" --at "2121 debug_grazes == 1" --at "2121 debug_fuel == 157" --expect "debug_state == 1" --expect "debug_rewinds == 3" --expect "debug_grazes == 1"
